WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.290
- Our next guest rocked it
at the 2008 Olympic games,

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.950
where she won gold on the balance beam.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.070
Then she rocked it on
"Dancing With The Stars"

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.290
when she took home the
mirror ball trophy in 2009,

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.098
let's say hello to Shawn
Johnson, everybody.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:19.240
(upbeat music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.080
All right, so first of all, hello, Shawn,

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.100
how ya doing?

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:22.933
- Great.

00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:24.870
How are you?
- I am doing really well.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.470
So which were you prouder of winning,

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.550
the Olympics or "Dancing With The Stars"?

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.130
And note, I might judge you
on this answer. (laughs)

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.420
- Honestly, probably
"Dancing With The Stars".

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.570
- Are you serious?

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.720
You can't be serious.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.060
- I am a like the shyest
person in the entire world.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:47.210
I knew I was like pretty
good at gymnastics.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.760
Like, you know, you can sing, right?

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.650
Yeah.
- I, I could not dance.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.910
I wanted to lock myself in a
bathroom and cry and go home.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.650
So when I won the mirror ball trophy,

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.780
I felt like I conquered Everest.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.810
- Oh, I love that.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:00.830
So it's like, basically that's,

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.720
it was more about the
emotional state of everything

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.930
and you accomplishing something
you never thought you would.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.420
Okay, I take my judgment back.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.314
Okay, I accept your answer.

00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:09.740
(laughs) So,

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.563
so what are the best and hardest
parts of parenting for you?

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.090
- Well, I have an 11 month old
daughter and she's my first.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.640
So everything is difficult, but
she is the light of my life.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.980
- So you basically don't sleep,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.840
that's what you're saying. (laughs)

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:25.673
- Yeah, never.

00:01:25.673 --> 00:01:28.083
I live off of coffee and caffeine.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.530
But, (stammers) you know with your kids,

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.610
it's just like seeing her
grow up and learn and smile

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:39.610
and love life with just such
innocent beauty is just,

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.210
it makes me love life even more.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.633
- They slow you down,
definitely, in a good way.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.100
So you recently partnered
up with Duracell.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.490
Can you tell us about that?

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:50.323
- Yeah.

00:01:50.323 --> 00:01:52.090
So, I mean, as a new mom,

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.950
I feel like you do
everything in your power

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.180
to protect your babies.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.010
And Duracell had approached us

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:58.670
and I was reading all of their research

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:01.320
and this story about Marisa and Cameron

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.860
and found out that lithium
batteries are so toxic

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.470
and dangerous to babies.

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:08.120
And I just felt like as a mom,

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.610
the fact that I didn't know about it

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.350
means I feel like a lot of
other moms don't know about it.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.000
So I was just trying to use,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.520
lend my voice in a platform

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.090
to share really educational
and great information.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.220
- I think that's amazing.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.980
We actually have a mom with us

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.640
who knows all too well
how terrifying it can be

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.810
to have a child swallow a coin battery.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:29.220
And you were just mentioning her name.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.680
So let's let's welcome, Marisa everybody.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.334
Hey, Marisa.

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:35.510
- Hi, Kelly.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.343
- Hi.

00:02:36.343 --> 00:02:39.630
So tell us what happened
with your son, Cameron.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:44.630
- So Cam is, he's our youngest of three,

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:48.120
and one, it was just a normal Saturday

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.190
and I was getting ready for
work and we were playing

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.130
and all of a sudden I just noticed

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.370
he stopped like singing with us.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:57.410
And I looked down at him

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.390
and he was just kind of hunched over

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:03.690
and I just knew something was wrong.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:07.540
And so, you know, we rushed
him, we got him in the car,

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.160
we rushed him to the emergency room

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.090
and they took x-rays and they found

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.540
that he had swallowed
a lithium coin battery

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.333
and he was rushed to the OR,

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.050
and it was a surgically removed.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:25.593
It was lodged in his esophagus
and it had burns inside.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.183
We were in the hospital for 4
1/2 to five months with him.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.090
And thank goodness now, a few years later,

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.940
he is doing great.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.820
I never knew how dangerous
these things were

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.790
in our everyday house, you
know, where kids can reach them

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.340
and it's just important to just educate

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.600
and share Cam's story
so everyone just knows

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.040
how dangerous it is in our homes

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.730
with our little babies running around.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.400
- I'm secretly panicking right now.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.290
'Cause you don't think
like, oh wait, well,

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.110
batteries are in everything.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:02.150
Like, you know, it's so hard.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:04.370
And my son, especially
my four year old boy,

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.460
loves to take things apart
and put it back together.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:08.540
Like, oh Lord.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.190
It's just such a scary thing.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:13.870
So, Shawn, what is Duracell
doing to help protect families?

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:15.410
Why'd you join up with them?

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:16.630
- Yeah, so like you were saying,

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:19.070
it was a panic attack from my end as well,

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.970
because you find these
lithium coin batteries

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.960
in thermometers and
sometimes birthday cards

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.860
and baby toys actually have them.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:29.470
So Duracell actually did this
new initiative and campaign

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.510
where they changed all the packaging.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:33.330
So it's like child-secure packaging.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.280
And then they also coated
these lithium coin batteries

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.860
in a non-toxic bitter coating,

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.100
so that if a baby goes to ingest it,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.060
it discourages them from swallowing it

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.510
and they'll spit it back out,
which is just another way

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.520
to kind of protect our little ones.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.890
- Wow, that's so clever.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.160
Like what a clever way to get around that

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.610
'cause they will spit it out.

